---
name: ingest
description: Load new data into the {{ project_name }} database, report what was added, and check the contract. Use when the user has new data, or before looking at the app when the data is stale.
when_to_use: >-
  Use when the user says things like "ingest", "load the new files", "update the data", "refresh the database".
argument-hint: "[files…]"
allowed-tools: Bash(uv run {{ project_name }} ingest *) Bash(uv run {{ project_name }} status){% if backup %} Bash(uv run {{ project_name }} backup) Bash(uv run {{ project_name }} status --remote){% endif %}
---

# Ingest

Files: $ARGUMENTS

1. `uv run {{ project_name }} status`: how fresh the data is now.
2. `uv run {{ project_name }} ingest <files>`.
3. Report the counts, every error, and the contract line. If the contract has problems, show them and stop.
{%- if backup %}
4. `uv run {{ project_name }} backup`, after every ingest that stored data, also when `ingest` exited 1. It is the
   one command that verifies the snapshot and, with `[backup] remote`, copies it to Cloud Storage and checks the
   MD5s. The `ingest` command itself makes no backup.
5. Report the "Backed up to …" line, and the "Copied to gs://…" line, or `uv run {{ project_name }} status --remote`
   ("Off-machine:"). If the copy failed, the local snapshot is safe: report the error (often an expired `gcloud`
   login), and run `backup` again once it is fixed. Never delete anything. If `[backup] remote` is not set, say
   that the backup is on this machine only, and offer `/backup setup-remote`.
6. If the app is running, tell the user to click *Reload data*.
{%- else %}
4. If the app is running, tell the user to click *Reload data*.
{%- endif %}
{%- if motherduck %} Do not publish: suggest `/publish` only if the user wants the copy current.{% endif %}

